# The operation takes its paths from the environment: no code decides them, so the files are known only by the
# variable that holds each (a hole the term names, never a guess). Three places all the same, by their variables;
# `read_pair` reads two and gives a str back to `join`, which writes the third.

route storage.run
step run/join
step run/join/read_pair

line entry > run call
line Disk(first) > run/join/read_pair own
line Disk(second) > run/join/read_pair own
line run/join/read_pair > run/join back
line run/join > Disk(destination) own

side entry left
side Disk(first) left
side Disk(second) left
side Disk(destination) right
